        {
          "path": "references/cloud-code-publish.md",
          "content": "# Verify Cloud Code Publishing\n\n## 云代码发布\n\nVerify MCP 常用工具：\n\n```text\nmcp__verify.publish_cloud_code_from_workspace\n```\n\n通用 payload：\n\n```json\n{\n  \"configId\": 44,\n  \"workspacePath\": \"/absolute/path/to/workspace/src\",\n  \"currentFilePath\": \"src/com/example/cloud/Entry.java\",\n  \"applyToConfig\": true,\n  \"compileSettings\": {\n    \"dexClassName\": \"com.example.cloud.Entry\",\n    \"dexMethodName\": \"main\",\n    \"dexMethodParamTypes\": [],\n    \"enableR8Obfuscation\": false,\n    \"enableBlackObfuscation\": false,\n    \"useLocalCache\": false\n  }\n}\n```\n\n建议：\n\n- 调试阶段关闭混淆和本地缓存。\n- 发布结果要记录 dex hash。\n- 每次功能迭代更新 `BUILD_LABEL` 或等价日志标签，便于确认设备实际运行的是新版本。\n- 编译失败先看 Java 语法、缺失 import、Verify SDK 类是否存在，再看混淆/缓存。\n\n发布前如果不确定编译入口、缓存、R8/Black 混淆、task 语义，先查：\n\n```text\nmcp__verify.get_compile_semantics\nmcp__verify.get_config\nmcp__verify.get_full_config_snapshot\n```\n\n\n"
        },
        {
          "path": "references/compile-troubleshooting.md",
          "content": "# Verify Compile Troubleshooting\n\n## Black 混淆 `IllegalArgumentException: Method code too large!`\n\n这是单个 Java 方法的 JVM `Code` 属性超过 65,535 字节，不是 Dex 的 65,536 方法引用数限制。\nBlack 混淆加入不透明条件、无效分支、异常路径、调度逻辑或花指令后，会放大原方法的字节码；\n大型 `switch`、巨型初始化方法、长数组/字符串常量、自动生成代码和本来就很长的业务方法最容易越界。\n转换器在写回 class 时通常由 ASM 抛出 `IllegalArgumentException: Method code too large!`。\n\n按以下顺序处理：\n\n1. 仅将 `enableBlackObfuscation=false` 后重编译。成功即可确认问题位于 Black 变换，不是\n   `useLocalCache`、资源 ZIP 或运行时加载。\n2. 从编译日志/堆栈定位具体类和方法；优先检查大 `switch`、静态初始化器 `<clinit>`、实例\n   初始化器、单方法内的大量常量和自动展开代码。\n3. 把超大方法拆成多个 helper 方法或类；把巨型表数据移到资源文件，避免在 `<clinit>` 中逐项\n   构造；拆分大 `switch` 或生成代码。\n4. 若 Black 支持强度和排除规则，降低该方法的变换强度，或将超大类/方法加入跳过列表。\n   R8 只有在 Black 之前确实缩小目标方法时才可能缓解；若 Black 先失败，后续收缩不会执行。\n5. 先用关闭 Black 的产物验证业务和入口，再逐步恢复混淆；每次记录任务 ID、配置 ID、开关和\n   报错方法，确认是哪条变换导致膨胀。\n\n`useLocalCache` 只控制宿主运行时 Dex 持久化，不参与 class 方法大小计算，切换它不会修复该\n异常。\n\n\n"
        },
        {
          "path": "references/core-and-tokens.md",
          "content": "# Verify Core And Tokens\n\n## 核心概念\n\nVerify 框架通常由两层组成：\n\n- **云代码 dex**：Java 源码编译成 dex，由 Verify/Xposed 注入宿主 app 后执行指定入口。\n- **资源 zip**：随配置下发的二进制/资源包，常用于 `.so`、`.jar`、配置、脚本和静态资源。\n\n工作原则：\n\n- 改业务模块代码时只改项目内 cloud-code/resource zip，不改 Verify 框架 APK。\n- 先更新资源 zip，再发布 cloud-code dex，避免新 dex 找不到新资源。\n- 发布后必须看设备日志和 app 私有 trace，不能只看编译成功。\n- 如果用户给了 configId、包名、入口类、workspace，直接沿用，不要重新猜。\n\n## Token 处理\n\nVerify MCP 分两类 token：\n\n```text\nVERIFY_API_TOKEN      应用、配置、卡密扩展、源码工作区、资源 zip、云代码编译发布、版本发布\nVERIFY_PROTECT_TOKEN  VMP、混淆、Dex2C、SO 保护、注入/加固任务\n```\n\n使用 Verify 工具前，优先调用：\n\n```text\nmcp__verify.server_info\n```\n\n查看 `tokens.apiToken.source` 和 `tokens.protectToken.source`。`source` 为 `missing` 表示当前 MCP 进程没有对应 token。\n\n如果缺少当前工具需要的 token，或者调用返回：\n\n```text\n当前工具需要配置环境变量 VERIFY_API_TOKEN\n当前工具需要配置环境变量 VERIFY_PROTECT_TOKEN\n401 / 403 / unauthorized / forbidden / token invalid\n```\n\n以及 `server_info` 显示仍在使用 `vat_xxx_replace_me`、`vpt_xxx_replace_me`、`vat_xxx`、`vpt_xxx` 这类占位 token 时，必须暂停当前 Verify 操作，直接向用户索要对应真实 token。不要猜 token，不要改用无关凭据，也不要假装已发布或已验证。\n\n用户提供后，用运行时切换工具写入当前 MCP 进程：\n\n```text\nmcp__verify.set_api_token      # 设置 VERIFY_API_TOKEN\nmcp__verify.set_protect_token  # 设置 VERIFY_PROTECT_TOKEN\n```\n\n然后从失败的原操作重试。只索要当前工具需要的 token 类型。\n\n## 项目识别清单\n\n开始发布前确认：\n\n```text\nconfigId: Verify 配置 id\npackageName: 宿主 app 包名\nworkspacePath: 云代码源码根目录\ncurrentFilePath: 入口 Java 文件相对路径\ndexClassName: 入口类全名\ndexMethodName: 入口静态方法名\ndexMethodParamTypes: 入口方法参数类型数组\nzipPath: 资源 zip 路径，若有资源变更\ntraceDir: 模块写入的 app 私有日志目录\n```\n\n典型入口：\n\n```java\npublic final class Entry {\n    public static void main() {\n        // Verify 调用入口\n    }\n}\n```\n\n\n"
        },
        {
          "path": "references/device-debugging.md",
          "content": "# Verify Device Debugging\n\n## 设备运行和日志验证\n\n常用 adb：\n\n```bash\nadb devices\nadb shell pidof <package>\nadb shell monkey -p <package> 1\nadb shell am force-stop <package>\nadb logcat -c\nadb logcat | rg \"<tag>|Verify|Hook|Crash|AndroidRuntime\"\n```\n\napp 私有 trace 一般需要 root：\n\n```bash\nadb shell su -c 'ls -lah /data/data/<package>/files'\nadb shell su -c 'tail -200 /data/data/<package>/files/<trace-dir>/runtime-YYYYMMDD.log' | tr -d '\\r'\nadb shell su -c 'tail -200 /data/data/<package>/files/<trace-dir>/native-YYYYMMDD.log' | tr -d '\\r'\n```\n\n验证点：\n\n- host 进程是否存在。\n- 日志里是否出现新 build label。\n- 云代码入口是否执行。\n- 资源 zip 是否匹配当前版本。\n- native/java hook 是否安装成功。\n- 如果崩溃，是否有 tombstone 或 Java stack。\n\n## app 私有目录 trace/dump 拉取\n\n把设备文件拉到工作目录：\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p device_dumps/<name>\nadb shell su -c 'tar -C /data/data/<package>/files/<trace-dir> -cf /data/local/tmp/<name>.tar .'\nadb pull /data/local/tmp/<name>.tar device_dumps/<name>/\ntar -xf device_dumps/<name>/<name>.tar -C device_dumps/<name>/\n```\n\n针对大目录，先在设备侧过滤：\n\n```bash\nadb shell su -c 'find /data/data/<package>/files/<trace-dir> -maxdepth 2 -type f | sort | tail -100' | tr -d '\\r'\n```\n\n## 常用 Verify 辅助 API\n\n常见类/方法名会随 Verify 版本变化，优先在项目源码或反编译框架里 `rg` 确认。\n\n常见能力：\n\n```java\nHookHelper.getUnzipDir();          // resource zip 解压目录\nHookHelper.clearZipCache();        // 清理 zip 缓存\nHookHelper.getHostClassLoader();   // 宿主 ClassLoader\nHookHelper.getModuleClassLoader(); // 模块/Verify ClassLoader，若当前版本提供\n```\n\n资源写入回调形态：\n\n```java\nResourceTaskManager.submitTask(new ResourceTaskCallback() {\n    @Override\n    public void onResourceWritten(ResourceTaskManager.ResourceTask task) {\n        // retry load resources/native\n    }\n}, false);\n```\n\n使用建议：\n\n- 资源可能晚于 cloud-code 入口可用；`main()` 执行不代表 resource zip 已落盘。\n- native/.so、bridge jar、配置文件等依赖资源的逻辑，应挂 `ResourceTaskManager.submitTask(callback, false)`，资源未就绪时等待回调，资源已就绪时回调会立即/很快执行。\n- UI 展示一般不需要等 hook/native 安装完成；具体功能执行前再检查 native ready 状态。\n- 不要无限主动轮询；高频轮询会拖慢宿主 app。\n- 不要只在启动瞬间尝试一次 `HookHelper.getUnzipDir()`；如果失败要等资源回调再重试。\n- 需要刷新 UI/状态时做局部更新，避免全局重建导致闪烁。\n\n## 常见问题\n\n### 发布成功但设备还是旧逻辑\n\n检查：\n\n- dex hash 是否变化。\n- `useLocalCache` 是否关闭。\n- build label 是否更新并出现在设备日志。\n- resource zip 是否也更新。\n- 是否需要重启宿主进程。\n- 如果多个渠道包要求 `dexHash` 完全一致，只编译一次并用 `apply_compile_task_to_configs` 批量应用完整产物；VMP 开启时该流程会同时绑定匹配的 Native Bundle。\n\n### resource zip 找不到文件\n\n检查：\n\n- `HookHelper.getUnzipDir()` 是否可用。\n- zip 内路径是否是 `payload/lib/<abi>/...` 或代码实际查找的路径。\n- ABI 是否匹配 `Build.SUPPORTED_ABIS`。\n- 是否需要在资源写入回调后再加载。\n- 是否调用了清理旧 zip cache。\n\n### 编译失败\n\n检查：\n\n- `workspacePath` 是否是源码根目录。\n- `currentFilePath` 是否相对 workspace 正确。\n- `dexClassName` 和 Java package/class 是否一致。\n- 入口方法是否 static，参数类型是否匹配。\n- 缺失 import 或 Verify SDK 类名是否写错。\n\n### 应用卡顿\n\n检查：\n\n- 是否高频主动调用 JS/反射/IO。\n- 是否全局重建 UI。\n- 是否大量写日志或 dump。\n- 是否在主线程做文件读写、压缩、反编译。\n\n替代方案：\n\n- 使用事件触发。\n- 做有限重试和退避。\n- 缓存上次结果，只在变化时刷新。\n- 后台线程写文件，UI 主线程只做最小更新。\n\n### 崩溃或自退\n\n区分：\n\n- Java crash：看 `AndroidRuntime`。\n- native crash：看 tombstone / signal。\n- 游戏自退：没有 tombstone，可能是 `finish`、`System.exit`、`killProcess` 或脚本检测。\n\n常用检查：\n\n```bash\nadb logcat -d | rg \"AndroidRuntime|FATAL EXCEPTION|tombstone|signal|DEBUG|crash\"\nadb shell su -c 'ls -lt /data/tombstones | head'\n```\n\n"
        },
        {
          "path": "references/dex-cache-runtime.md",
          "content": "# Verify Dex Cache Runtime\n\n## `useLocalCache` / `UseLocalCache` 语义\n\n### 定义\n\n`useLocalCache` 是 Verify MCP 编译/更新接口使用的字段名，写入配置 JSON 后对应\n`dexData.UseLocalCache`。它控制的是宿主运行时是否持久保存 Dex，并在下次启动时优先执行该\nDex；它不是服务端编译缓存，也不负责复用 R8/BlackObfuscator 的编译产物。\n\n- `useLocalCache=true`：下载 Dex 后，把 Dex、入口信息和 `dexHash` 持久化到宿主 app 私有\n  `SharedPreferences`。宿主下次启动时先执行缓存 Dex，再异步请求服务器配置，因此入口通常\n  比等待网络下载更早执行。\n- `useLocalCache=false`：不把新下载的 Dex 作为跨进程/跨启动缓存保留。正常无缓存状态下，\n  每次启动都要先请求服务器并取得 Dex，随后才执行入口。\n\n调试阶段通常设为 `false`，目的是避免宿主启动时先执行上一个版本的 Dex，使日志和设备行为\n更容易与当前发布的 `dexHash`、`BUILD_LABEL` 对齐。需要尽早执行稳定版本 Dex 时再设为\n`true`。\n\n### 缓存内容与位置\n\n当前 Xposed 和 Inject 模板保存以下四项：\n\n- Dex 的 Base64 数据：`cachedDex`\n- 入口类名：`cachedDexClassName`\n- 入口方法名：`cachedDexMethodName`\n- Dex 内容 Hash：`cachedDexHash`\n\n数据通过宿主 `Context.getSharedPreferences(..., MODE_PRIVATE)` 写入宿主 app 私有目录：\n\n- Xposed 模板的 preferences 名称：`ITHookConfig`\n- Inject 模板的 preferences 名称：`InjectConfig`\n\n这是 Dex 持久缓存，不是把源码工作区或云端编译任务缓存在本机电脑上。\n\n### 启动、校验与刷新顺序\n\n启用缓存后的运行顺序如下：\n\n1. 宿主进程启动，运行时读取 `cachedDex`、缓存入口类和入口方法。\n2. 缓存完整且可解码时，立即把它交给 Dex 执行器。\n3. 运行时并行请求服务器配置，读取服务器返回的 `dexHash` 和 `UseLocalCache`。\n4. `serverDexHash` 与 `cachedDexHash` 不同时，下载新 Dex。\n5. 开关仍为 `true` 时，用新 Dex、入口信息和 Hash 覆盖本地缓存，并提示重启以确保新逻辑\n   完整生效。\n6. 配置请求持续失败、运行时异常达到清理条件，或验证流程要求终止当前加载时，模板会清理\n   Dex 缓存。\n\n因此，`dexHash` 是运行时判断缓存版本是否过期的关键字段。排查旧逻辑时应同时核对服务端\n`dexHash`、本地 `cachedDexHash`、运行日志中的 `BUILD_LABEL`，以及宿主进程是否已重启。\n\n这里的“优先执行”是严格的启动顺序：缓存 Dex 可能早于本次服务器配置响应、开关更新和\n验证结果执行。当前模板启动读取时只检查 Base64 是否可解码以及入口类/方法是否存在，不会\n重新计算 Dex 内容 Hash 并与 `cachedDexHash` 比较；`cachedDexHash` 当前主要用于和服务端\n`dexHash` 做版本比较，不是本地完整性校验结果。\n\n### 与其它缓存的区别\n\n以下缓存彼此独立：\n\n- **Dex 本地缓存**：由 `useLocalCache` 控制，内容是 Dex、入口类、入口方法和 `dexHash`。\n- **Resource zip 状态/缓存**：使用独立的 `cachedZipHash`、解压目录和\n  `HookHelper.clearZipCache()`；不受 `useLocalCache` 控制。\n- **宿主 app `cacheDir` / `codeCacheDir`**：常用于复制 `.so`、bridge jar 和\n  `DexClassLoader` 优化文件，不受该开关直接控制。\n- **云代码编辑器缓存**：服务端 `EditorCache` 或前端浏览器本地存储中的源码快照；\n  `cloudCode.exists=true` 只表示编辑快照存在。\n- **编译任务/产物**：`SUCCESS`、`downloaded`、R8/Black 混淆输出属于编译任务语义；\n  `useLocalCache=true` 不会让多次编译得到相同 `dexHash`。\n\n### 当前模板的切换边界\n\n当前 Xposed/Inject 模板只在重新下载 Dex 的分支中根据 `UseLocalCache=false` 清理已有 Dex\n缓存。若只把开关从 `true` 改成 `false`，但服务端 `dexHash` 没有变化，Hash 比较可能直接命中\n旧缓存，清理分支不会执行，旧 Dex 仍可能在后续启动时被优先执行。\n\n缓存 preferences 名称和键是宿主 app 级固定值，当前没有按 `configId`、目标 app 版本或进程\n分别命名。同一宿主数据目录切换匹配配置时，服务器 Hash 校验最终会触发刷新，但旧缓存仍可能\n在新配置响应返回前先执行一次。\n\n关闭已启用的缓存时，应完成以下任一操作并重启宿主进程：\n\n- 同时发布一个 `dexHash` 发生变化的新 Dex，让运行时进入下载和清理分支。\n- 在运行时代码中显式调用对应的 `clearDexCache()`。\n- 明确删除宿主 preferences 中的 `cachedDex`、`cachedDexClassName`、\n  `cachedDexMethodName`、`cachedDexHash`。\n\n长期实现上，配置处理逻辑应在检测到 `UseLocalCache=false` 时直接清理持久 Dex 缓存，不应把\n清理动作依赖于 `dexHash` 是否变化。\n\n\n"
        },
        {
          "path": "references/heartbeat-verification.md",
          "content": "# Verify Heartbeat Usage\n\n## Usage Boundaries\n\nUse this reference to help a developer call the existing heartbeat API and consume its results.\n\n- Heartbeat is started explicitly by developer code.\n- Heartbeat supports time cards.\n- Ordinary card verification and heartbeat are independent choices.\n- Existing code that only performs ordinary verification does not need heartbeat changes.\n- Heartbeat is available from Standalone ITHook, Embedded Patch Runtime, and Inject when the\n  matching current development dependency is used.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nImport the public API:\n\n```java\nimport com.xy.verify.heartbeat.Heartbeat;\nimport com.xy.verify.heartbeat.HeartbeatListener;\nimport com.xy.verify.heartbeat.HeartbeatSession;\nimport com.xy.verify.heartbeat.HeartbeatState;\n\nimport java.util.Map;\n```\n\nConnect with an explicit card code:\n\n```java\nHeartbeatSession heartbeatSession = Heartbeat.connect(cardCode, new HeartbeatListener() {\n    @Override\n    public void onConnected(Map<String, Object> data, String dataVersion) {\n        Object featureValue = data.get(\"feature\");\n        // Continue the feature after heartbeat is connected.\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void onDataChanged(Map<String, Object> data, String dataVersion) {\n        // Refresh values that the application owner changed.\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void onAuthorizationLost(String code, String message, Map<String, Object> data) {\n        // Stop the protected feature or return to the verification screen.\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void onStateChanged(HeartbeatState state) {\n        // Update local behavior from the state examples below.\n    }\n});\n```\n\nUse a card already saved by the normal verification flow:\n\n```java\nHeartbeatSession heartbeatSession = Heartbeat.connectSavedCard(listener);\n```\n\nUse `connectSavedCard()` only after the normal card flow has stored a valid time card. Use\n`connect(cardCode, listener)` when the developer already has the card string.\n\n## Session Usage\n\nRead the current state and latest data:\n\n```java\nHeartbeatState state = heartbeatSession.state();\nMap<String, Object> latestData = heartbeatSession.latestData();\n```\n\nStop the session when the feature no longer needs heartbeat:\n\n```java\nheartbeatSession.stop();\n```\n\nKeep the `HeartbeatSession` in a component with an appropriate lifetime, such as a feature\ncontroller or application service. Avoid storing it in short-lived local variables when later\nstate inspection or stopping is required.\n\nCalling connect again for the same card can be used to attach another listener to the active\nsession. Avoid creating listeners repeatedly from every Activity recreation.\n\n## Callback Usage\n\n### `onConnected(data, dataVersion)`\n\nUse this callback as the successful connection entry point. Read heartbeat-channel return data\nfrom `data`. Keep `dataVersion` only when the application needs to compare or display data\nrevisions.\n\n### `onDataChanged(data, dataVersion)`\n\nUse this callback to refresh feature switches, text, configuration, or other values supplied by\nthe application owner. Treat `data` as read-only.\n\n### `onAuthorizationLost(code, message, data)`\n\nUse this callback for an explicit authorization failure. Stop or disable the protected feature,\npresent the business message when appropriate, and consume any configured failure return data.\n\n### `onStateChanged(state)`\n\nHandle only the states relevant to the product experience:\n\n```java\n@Override\npublic void onStateChanged(HeartbeatState state) {\n    switch (state) {\n        case CONNECTED:\n            onHeartbeatAvailable();\n            break;\n        case NETWORK_GRACE:\n            showTemporaryNetworkState();\n            break;\n        case NETWORK_LOST:\n            onHeartbeatNetworkLost();\n            break;\n        case AUTHORIZATION_LOST:\n            onHeartbeatAuthorizationLost();\n            break;\n        case PROTOCOL_ERROR:\n            recordHeartbeatError();\n            break;\n        case STOPPED:\n            clearHeartbeatUi();\n            break;\n        case CONNECTING:\n        default:\n            showHeartbeatConnecting();\n            break;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nHeartbeat callbacks run on a background thread. Post UI work to the Android main thread:\n\n```java\nnew Handler(Looper.getMainLooper()).post(() -> updateUi(data));\n```\n\nKeep callback bodies small. Dispatch longer business work to the application's own executor.\n\n## Reading Return Data\n\nRead values defensively because application owners can change return-data content:\n\n```java\nObject rawEnabled = data.get(\"enabled\");\nboolean enabled = rawEnabled instanceof Boolean && (Boolean) rawEnabled;\n\nObject rawTitle = data.get(\"title\");\nString title = rawTitle == null ? \"\" : String.valueOf(rawTitle);\n```\n\nFor nested objects, check the runtime type before casting:\n\n```java\nObject rawConfig = data.get(\"config\");\nif (rawConfig instanceof Map) {\n    Map<?, ?> config = (Map<?, ?>) rawConfig;\n    Object mode = config.get(\"mode\");\n}\n```\n\nDo not mutate the returned map or nested collections. Copy the values into application-owned\nmodels when local mutation is needed.\n\n## Configuring Return Data\n\nApplication owners configure global return data on the callback page and card-specific data on\nthe card management page.\n\nChoose a result condition:\n\n```text\nALWAYS        Return for success and failure\nSUCCESS_ONLY  Return only after success\nFAILURE_ONLY  Return only after failure\n```\n\nChoose a return channel:\n\n```text\nVERIFY_ONLY     Ordinary card verification only\nHEARTBEAT_ONLY  Heartbeat only\nBOTH            Ordinary verification and heartbeat\n```\n\nCommon choices:\n\n| Requirement | Result condition | Return channel |\n|---|---|---|\n| Return feature data after heartbeat connects | `SUCCESS_ONLY` | `HEARTBEAT_ONLY` |\n| Return the same successful data to both flows | `SUCCESS_ONLY` | `BOTH` |\n| Return an error hint after heartbeat authorization fails | `FAILURE_ONLY` | `HEARTBEAT_ONLY` |\n| Always return a shared field in heartbeat | `ALWAYS` | `HEARTBEAT_ONLY` |\n\nHeartbeat clients receive only fields assigned to the heartbeat channel. A missing field commonly\nmeans its channel, result condition, or card-level enable switch does not match the current event.\n\n## MCP Usage\n\nUse these Verify MCP tools when they are available:\n\n```text\nget_verification_examples\nupdate_app_redeem_extra\nupdate_card_extra\n```\n\nUse `get_verification_examples` to obtain the current public examples for the selected application.\n\nConfigure global heartbeat data with `redeemExtraV2`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"feature\": {\n    \"value\": true,\n    \"mode\": \"SUCCESS_ONLY\",\n    \"channel\": \"HEARTBEAT_ONLY\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nConfigure card-specific heartbeat data with these fields:\n\n```text\nextra\nextraEnabled\nextraResultMode\nextraChannelMode\n```\n\nSet `extraEnabled=true`, select the desired result mode, and use `HEARTBEAT_ONLY` or `BOTH` for a\ncard value that should reach heartbeat callbacks.\n\n## Recommended Integration Patterns\n\n### Start After User Verification\n\n```java\nvoid onCardVerified(String cardCode) {\n    heartbeatSession = Heartbeat.connect(cardCode, heartbeatListener);\n}\n```\n\n### Restore From A Saved Card\n\n```java\nvoid startFeature() {\n    heartbeatSession = Heartbeat.connectSavedCard(heartbeatListener);\n}\n```\n\n### Stop With The Feature\n\n```java\nvoid stopFeature() {\n    if (heartbeatSession != null) {\n        heartbeatSession.stop();\n        heartbeatSession = null;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nDo not stop the session for a routine Activity recreation when the protected feature should remain\nactive. Tie it to the feature's actual lifetime.\n\n## Usage Troubleshooting\n\n- Connection immediately reports authorization loss: check that the card is a valid time card for\n  the current application and device.\n- `connectSavedCard()` reports an input or protocol error: complete the normal card flow first or\n  call `connect(cardCode, listener)` with the explicit card.\n- Data is empty after connection: check global/card return data, `extraEnabled`, result condition,\n  and whether the channel is `HEARTBEAT_ONLY` or `BOTH`.\n- `onDataChanged()` is not called: change a heartbeat-visible return field and wait for the next\n  successful update; use `latestData()` to inspect the current snapshot.\n- UI access throws a thread exception: post UI operations to the main looper.\n- Callbacks appear more than once: keep one listener per feature lifetime and avoid registering a\n  new anonymous listener after every Activity recreation.\n- Feature remains active after `NETWORK_LOST` or `AUTHORIZATION_LOST`: implement the desired product\n  behavior in the corresponding callback/state branch.\n\n## Usage Acceptance\n\nVerify these behaviors in the target Runtime:\n\n1. A valid time card reaches `CONNECTED` and invokes `onConnected()`.\n2. Initial heartbeat return data is readable and matches the configured channel.\n3. Updating a heartbeat-visible value invokes `onDataChanged()` with the new snapshot.\n4. Temporary network interruption reaches the expected network state and the application handles\n   it without UI-thread errors.\n5. Card disable, expiry, or unbind invokes `onAuthorizationLost()` and stops the protected feature.\n6. `latestData()` matches the last delivered data.\n7. `stop()` reaches `STOPPED` and the feature releases its session reference.\n8. Activity recreation does not multiply listeners or duplicate business actions.\n"
        },
        {
          "path": "references/local-patch-runtime.md",
          "content": "# Verify App Local Patch Runtime\n\n## Scope\n\nUse this reference for Verify App's local APK Patch flow, the embedded NPatch Runtime, and cached cloud Dex health isolation. The standalone ITHook module and Inject products have separate build paths.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe local Patch output executes this chain inside the patched host:\n\n```text\npatched host APK\n  -> NPatch meta loader / native loader\n  -> loader.bin\n  -> VerifyRuntimeInitializer\n  -> per-app Verify configuration request\n  -> cached or downloaded cloud Hook Dex\n```\n\nRelevant workspace paths:\n\n- `verfiy_app`: Android client and local Patch UI/orchestration.\n- `verfiy_app/npatch-engine`: APK patch engine bundled into Verify App.\n- `patch`: local NPatch source, including `patch-loader` and `meta-loader`.\n- `Template/verfiy_hook_embedded`: Verify Runtime Java source compiled directly into `loader.bin`.\n- `Template/verfiy_hook`: standalone ITHook module APK/AAR source; keep it independent.\n- `Template/verfiy_inject`: Dex Inject product; it is not the local Patch Runtime.\n\nLocal Patch embeds Runtime capability, not a fixed business Hook Dex. The patched host requests its configured cloud Dex at runtime using its app configuration and then invokes the configured entry class/method.\n\n## Build And Synchronize\n\nAfter changing `Template/verfiy_hook_embedded`, rebuild and synchronize Runtime assets before building Verify App:\n\n```bash\ncd verfiy_app\n./npatch-engine/sync-runtime.sh\n```\n\nThat script:\n\n1. Builds `patch-loader` and `meta-loader` from local `patch` source.\n2. Compiles embedded Verify Java sources into `patch/out/assets/release/npatch/loader.bin`.\n3. Synchronizes `loader.bin`, `metaloader.dex`, and four ABI variants of `libnpatch.so` into `verfiy_app/npatch-engine/src/main/assets/npatch`.\n4. Builds the embedded ITHook APK and extracts fixed Verify native assets for `arm64-v8a`, `armeabi-v7a`, `x86`, and `x86_64`.\n\n`verfiy_app/build.sh` runs this synchronization automatically before assembling the release APK. Use it for a full Verify App build; use `sync-runtime.sh` for a Runtime-only refresh.\n\nFor standalone ITHook verification, build separately:\n\n```bash\ncd Template/verfiy_hook\n./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest :app:assembleRelease\n```\n\n## Cached Dex Health Isolation\n\nPersistent health isolation applies only when `UseLocalCache=true`.\n\nState sequence:\n\n1. Immediately before invoking the cloud Dex entry, Runtime creates and locks an attempt marker containing Dex Hash, start time, and execution stage.\n2. After the entry returns, the marker remains locked for a 10-second health window.\n3. A healthy window deletes the marker and clears the pending failure count for the same Hash.\n4. A caught entry exception retains the marker with stage `ENTRY_THROWN`; a crash, process exit, force-stop, or system kill during the health window also leaves the marker behind.\n5. On the next process start, Runtime recovers an unlocked marker and atomically increments the persistent failure count for that Hash.\n6. First consecutive failure: clear only the matching cached Dex, redownload/retry the same server Hash, and do not quarantine it.\n7. Second consecutive failure of the same Hash: clear the matching cache, write the quarantine Hash, skip that server Dex version, and show the recovery notice once.\n8. A healthy run or a different server Dex Hash clears the pending count. A new server Hash also clears the old quarantine.\n\nThe intentional Verify restart action writes a one-use marker. On the following start it consumes that marker and discards the unfinished attempt without incrementing the failure count. Other process exits remain observable failures, so the two-strike threshold reduces incidental false positives.\n\nIsolation state lives under the patched host app's private files directory in `ithook_dex_guard`. Failure-state updates use a file lock and atomic replacement so multiple host processes do not lose increments or clear a newer Hash state.\n\nCore implementation and tests:\n\n- `Template/verfiy_hook_embedded/app/src/main/java/com/xy/ithook/core/DexExecutionGuard.java`\n- `Template/verfiy_hook_embedded/app/src/main/java/com/xy/ithook/remote/HookConfigService.java`\n- `Template/verfiy_hook_embedded/app/src/test/java/com/xy/ithook/core/DexExecutionGuardTest.java`\n\n## Verification\n\nRun focused tests before synchronizing Runtime:\n\n```bash\ncd Template/verfiy_hook_embedded\n./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest --tests com.xy.ithook.core.DexExecutionGuardTest\n```\n\nAfter synchronization, verify assets exist and changed as expected:\n\n```bash\nshasum -a 256 \\\n  patch/out/assets/release/npatch/loader.bin \\\n  verfiy_app/npatch-engine/src/main/assets/npatch/loader.bin\n\nfind verfiy_app/npatch-engine/src/main/assets/npatch/so -type f -name 'libnpatch.so' -print\nfind verfiy_app/npatch-engine/src/main/assets/verify/so -type f -name '*.so' -print\n```\n\nThe two `loader.bin` hashes must match. Confirm all requested ABIs are present, then build Verify App or patch a small fixture APK and inspect Runtime logs for first-failure retry versus second-failure quarantine behavior.\n\nDo not infer a Dex failure solely from an unrelated crash report. Correlate the isolated Hash, execution stage, attempt time, cached Hash, server Hash, and host process exit evidence.\n"
        },
        {
          "path": "references/local-protection.md",
          "content": "# Verify Local Protection Pattern\n\nUse this reference when a Verify cloud-code feature needs stronger client-side protection while\nkeeping the ordinary Verify endpoint unchanged. The pattern is designed for Hook, Inject, and\nembedded runtimes and is independent of any one game or UI template.\n\n## Trust Model\n\nTreat local Java, injected JavaScript, UI callbacks, and SharedPreferences as separate layers.\nThe UI callback is a notification layer, not the authority that grants a feature. The protected\nfeature should become available only after the internal verification result, an active lease, and\nthe runtime handshake all agree.\n\nClient-side checks increase tamper cost and reduce the useful lifetime of a bypass. They do not\nreplace server authorization. Prefer the Verify Heartbeat Runtime API when the current runtime\nand card type support it; use the local lease pattern below as a compatibility layer or offline\ngrace mechanism.\n\n## Layered Authorization\n\nUse four independent states:\n\n1. `VERIFIED`: the normal Verify response was decrypted and accepted by the internal card flow.\n2. `LEASE_VALID`: a short-lived local lease is valid for the current device and build.\n3. `SCRIPT_VALID`: the current return-data payload has the expected version, digest, and build\n   binding.\n4. `RUNTIME_READY`: the Java-to-JavaScript handshake completed for the current script generation.\n\nDo not collapse all four states into one public boolean. Keep the checks at separate boundaries:\n\n- The card implementation records `VERIFIED` before invoking the UI callback.\n- The entry class checks `VERIFIED` and `LEASE_VALID` before scheduling protected hooks.\n- The script registry checks `SCRIPT_VALID` before accepting remote JavaScript.\n- Feature commands check `RUNTIME_READY` immediately before dispatch.\n\n## Lease Construction\n\nWhen Heartbeat is unavailable, create a short local lease after a successful internal Verify\nresponse. Bind the lease to:\n\n```text\nmachine_hash\nextra_digest\nbuild_label\nverified_at\nlease_until\n```\n\nProtect the canonical value with an Android Keystore HMAC. A practical default is 2 hours for a\ntest environment and 4 hours for a production feature. A longer lease improves long-session\ncontinuity but increases the time a revoked or modified client can keep using local state.\n\nValidate all of the following on every protected boundary:\n\n- lease expiration;\n- device or machine-code change;\n- clock rollback;\n- build-label change;\n- HMAC mismatch;\n- host package mismatch.\n\nWhen the lease fails, clear the script registry and revoke new feature commands. Keep the process\nalive so the user can re-verify cleanly.\n\n## Heartbeat Renewal\n\nIf the Heartbeat API is available, keep a single `HeartbeatSession` for the feature lifetime:\n\n- start it after ordinary verification stores the time card;\n- process `onConnected` and `onDataChanged` inside the protected controller;\n- handle `onAuthorizationLost` by revoking the feature lease and clearing remote scripts;\n- treat `NETWORK_GRACE` and `NETWORK_LOST` according to the product's grace policy;\n- stop the session when the feature or host process ends.\n\nIf only ordinary verification is available, a silent renewal task may repeat the existing Verify\ncall. The renewal task must consume the internal result directly; do not route renewal authority\nthrough `onVerifySuccess` or a menu callback. A failed renewal can keep the current lease until\nits normal deadline, while an explicit authorization failure revokes it immediately.\n\n## Java/JavaScript Handshake\n\nFor each script generation, Java generates a fresh random nonce and passes it through ordinary\nruntime placeholders. The bootstrap script returns the nonce and generation through an existing\nruntime bridge. Java accepts the acknowledgement only when both values match:\n\n```text\nJava: generation + nonce -> bootGuard\nJavaScript: nonce + generation -> runtime bridge\nJava: accept acknowledgement -> RUNTIME_READY\n```\n\nUse a generation counter so an acknowledgement from an old payload cannot authorize a new one.\nGate feature commands on the accepted generation, not merely on the presence of a JavaScript\nobject. During migration, detect whether the payload contains the handshake placeholders; old\npayloads can use a compatibility path until the new return data is published.\n\n## Low-Noise Integrity Sampling\n\nAdd small, independently callable integrity samplers rather than one obvious `antiDebug()`\nfunction. Sample at a jittered interval and keep the result in protected runtime state. Useful\nlow-false-positive signals include:\n\n- debugger attachment or a non-zero process tracer;\n- unexpected host package or class-loader state;\n- missing expected entry methods or script generations;\n- a verification callback sequence with no matching internal result;\n- a changed build label or script digest.\n\nDo not display detection reasons in the menu, crash the host, or emit a distinctive public error\nbranch. On a failed sample, revoke the feature lease, stop new commands, and write a compact\nreason to the existing project telemetry channel. Keep ordinary diagnostic logs separate from\nthe protection signal so normal debugging remains useful.\n\n## Multi-Point Command Gates\n\nApply the final gate at real capability boundaries:\n\n- core Hook installation;\n- JavaScript bootstrap and core script installation;\n- feature-state submission;\n- dungeon/activity catalog requests;\n- dungeon start/cancel commands;\n- high-value feature actions.\n\nEach boundary should independently check the lease and current runtime generation. Avoid a single\npositive gate that every method calls and that can be replaced with a constant return value.\nNegative state transitions should clear the script registry and invalidate the current handshake.\n\n## Return-Data Design\n\nKeep dynamic fields separated by channel and scope:\n\n- application-level return data for shared production configuration;\n- card-scoped return data for a test card or an individual override;\n- heartbeat-only fields for live authorization state;\n- Verify-only fields for ordinary verification.\n\nUse version, build, expiration, and digest metadata around JavaScript payloads. Preserve existing\nlog-upload fields when merging return data. A successful DEX compile or a changed return-data\nrecord alone does not prove that the device executed the new protection version; verify both sides.\n\n## Protection Scope\n\nProtect the authorization and runtime core with VMP/Black/R8 according to the project policy:\n\n```text\nCard implementation\nLease/HMAC state\nRuntime handshake\nScript registry\nEntry and feature bridge\nRenewal/Heartbeat controller\n```\n\nKeep ordinary UI classes outside VMP when UI latency matters, while retaining R8 and Black for\nthose classes. Do not put the only copy of a critical decision in the UI layer.\n\n## Rollout and Verification\n\n1. Add the local lease and internal result path.\n2. Add handshake placeholders to a versioned test payload.\n3. Compile the matching cloud-code DEX and run focused Java/JavaScript tests.\n4. Apply the Test DEX and card-scoped return data separately.\n5. Confirm logs show the new build label, script version, generation, and handshake acceptance.\n6. Test lease expiration, clock rollback, altered `extra`, stale generation, and renewal failure.\n7. Publish production DEX and production return data only after Test verification.\n\nKeep rollback artifacts for both the DEX and return-data layers. A DEX rollback does not restore a\ncard-scoped JavaScript payload, and a return-data rollback does not restore a DEX lease policy.\n"
        },
        {
          "path": "references/mcp-tools.md",
          "content": "# Verify MCP Tools\n\n## Verify MCP 工具速查\n\n当用户问“哪个工具能拿示例函数调用/文档”时，优先使用这些文档类工具：\n\n```text\nserver_info                       # 查看后端地址、MCP 版本和 token 来源\nset_api_token                     # 当前 MCP 进程设置 VERIFY_API_TOKEN\nset_protect_token                 # 当前 MCP 进程设置 VERIFY_PROTECT_TOKEN\nclear_runtime_tokens              # 清除运行时 token，恢复环境变量 token\nget_verification_examples        # 获取普通验卡和心跳的当前公开调用示例\nget_card_verification_guide      # 卡密校验开关、自定义卡密逻辑共存语义\nget_runtime_api_doc              # 指定 runtime/class/method 的 API 文档\nlist_runtime_api_classes         # 列出 Xposed/Inject 运行时公开类\nget_runtime_lifecycle_guide      # main()/Activity/资源回调/线程兜底生命周期\nget_runtime_migration_guide      # 运行时迁移说明\nget_resource_and_native_rules    # resHook.zip、解压目录、资源回调、.so 加载建议\nget_compile_semantics            # 编译/缓存/入口/应用配置语义\ndownload_menupro_java_ui_template # 下载并解压 MenuPro 纯 Java UI 模板源码\n```\n\n配置与现状确认：\n\n```text\nserver_info\nget_context\nlist_apps\nlist_configs\nget_config\nget_full_config_snapshot\nget_config_files\nget_source_workspace\nget_cloud_code\nget_app_credentials\n```\n\n崩溃查询与下载：\n\n```text\nlist_runtime_crashes             # 按应用、类型、归因、关键字和时间查询问题组\nget_runtime_crash_events         # 按 fingerprint 读取组内事件与脱敏栈\ndownload_runtime_crash_report    # 下载 raw/event/group，默认本地落盘且不返回 Base64\n```\n\n`download_runtime_crash_report` 的 `type=raw`/`event` 需要 `eventId`，`type=group`\n需要 `fingerprint`。默认目录是 `~/.cache/verify-mcp/downloads/runtime-crashes`；仅在明确需要内联内容时设置\n`includeBase64=true`。\n\n资源/云代码/发布：\n\n```text\nupdate_config_files\ninstall_shadowhook\ninstall_wifi_adb_module\npush_source_workspace\npush_cloud_code\npublish_cloud_code_from_workspace\npublish_cloud_code\npublish_native_workspace\ncompile_config\ncreate_release\nbind_release_artifact\npublish_release\nrollback_release\n```\n\n任务查询和产物下载：\n\n```text\nlist_compile_tasks\nget_compile_task\nwait_compile_result\ndownload_compile_task\ndelete_compile_task\nlist_protect_tasks\nget_protect_task\ndownload_protect_task\ndelete_protect_task\ndownload_artifact\n```\n\n加固/保护任务：\n\n```text\nsubmit_build_task\nwait_build_task\nsubmit_inject_protect_task\nsubmit_obfuscate_protect_task\nsubmit_dex2c_protect_task\nsubmit_so_protect_task\nsubmit_vmp_protect_task\n```\n\n创建/维护配置：\n\n```text\ncreate_config\ncreate_module_config\nupdate_config\nupdate_compile_settings\ndelete_config\ndelete_module_config\napply_compile_task_to_config\napply_compile_task_to_configs\nsync_legacy_hook_runtime\n```\n\n卡密/兑换扩展字段：\n\n```text\nupdate_card_extra                # 单卡 extra、启用状态、结果条件和返回通道\nupdate_app_redeem_extra          # 全局字段级 mode/channel；优先使用 redeemExtraV2\n```\n\n心跳回参使用两个正交维度：`ALWAYS/SUCCESS_ONLY/FAILURE_ONLY` 与\n`VERIFY_ONLY/HEARTBEAT_ONLY/BOTH`。读取 `heartbeat-verification.md` 后再修改这些字段；\n保留旧 `redeemExtra`、`returnExtra` 的 VERIFY-only 兼容语义。\n\n布局/包校验：\n\n```text\nvalidate_cloud_code_layout\nvalidate_cloud_runtime\nvalidate_native_package\nsimulate_resource_layout\nsimulate_native_runtime_layout\nget_resource_and_native_rules\n```\n"
        },
        {
          "path": "references/menupro-integration.md",
          "content": "# Verify MenuPro Integration\n\n## MenuPro Java UI 模板联动\n\n当目标是给 Verify 云代码增加卡密验证、悬浮菜单或游戏辅助 UI 时，联动使用 `menupro-java-ui-template`。\n\n拉取模板源码：\n\n```json\n{\n  \"targetDir\": \"<verify-workspace>/src\",\n  \"profile\": \"verify-cloud\",\n  \"overwrite\": false\n}\n```\n\n工具语义：\n\n- `download_menupro_java_ui_template` 会从默认源码包地址下载 `menupro-java-ui-template.zip`，校验 sha256，解压到 `targetDir`，并清理临时 zip。\n- 模板 zip 默认包含 `com/xy/menupro/...`，所以 Verify 云代码通常把 `targetDir` 指到源码根 `workspace/src`。\n- `profile=verify-cloud` 会移除演示 `MainActivity.java` 和 `FloatingMenuService.java`，避免云代码扫描时引入 AndroidX 或 Manifest 依赖。\n- 如果是普通 Android app 项目而不是 Verify 云代码，可传 `targetDir=app/src/main/java` 并保留 `profile=full`。\n\nVerify 接入原则：\n\n- UI 入口放到 `ActivityTaskManager` 回调里，等待当前 Activity 可用后再挂 `InAppHost`。\n- 不要在 `main()` 里直接弹 Dialog 或创建悬浮菜单；`main()` 执行时前台 Activity 可能还没有稳定。\n- DEX Inject 侧使用 `com.xy.verfiy_inject.activity.ActivityTaskManager`；Xposed 侧使用对应 `com.xy.ithook.activity.ActivityTaskManager`。\n- 不要混用 `InjectHelper` 与 `HookHelper`。\n- MenuPro 的用户文案仍按模板规则写“星钥”“点亮”“解绑”等用户语言，不写接口地址、签名、机器码、类名或方法名。\n\n最小入口示例（DEX Inject）：\n\n```java\npackage com.example.cloud;\n\nimport android.app.Activity;\nimport android.widget.FrameLayout;\n\nimport com.xy.menupro.floating.FloatingController;\nimport com.xy.menupro.floating.InAppHost;\nimport com.xy.verfiy_inject.activity.ActivityLifecycleState;\nimport com.xy.verfiy_inject.activity.ActivityTaskManager;\n\npublic final class Entry {\n    private static volatile FloatingController controller;\n\n    public static void main() {\n        ActivityTaskManager.submitTask((activity, task) -> showMenu(activity),\n                ActivityLifecycleState.ON_RESUME, true);\n    }\n\n    private static void showMenu(Activity activity) {\n        if (controller != null) {\n            return;\n        }\n        FrameLayout content = activity.findViewById(android.R.id.content);\n        controller = new FloatingController(activity, new InAppHost(content));\n        content.post(() -> controller.show());\n    }\n}\n```\n\n发布顺序：\n\n1. 用 `download_menupro_java_ui_template` 拉取模板到云代码源码根。\n2. 修改 `CardKeyApiClient.java`、`CardKeyGateView.java`、`MenuPanelView.java` 等模板文件。\n3. 用 `publish_cloud_code_from_workspace` 扫描并编译。\n4. 需要写回配置时传 `applyToConfig=true`。\n5. 如果同时改了资源 zip，仍然先更新资源，再发布 dex。\n\n\n"
        },
        {
          "path": "references/multi-config-publishing.md",
          "content": "# Verify Multi-Config Publishing\n\n## 多配置完整编译产物发布\n\n同一套云代码需要推送到多个渠道包或多个 Verify 配置时，只编译一次，然后批量应用完整编译产物。不要对每个配置分别重新编译混淆。\n\n完整编译产物包括：\n\n- 编译后的 DEX 及其 `dexHash`\n- 启用 VMP 时与该 DEX 严格匹配的 Native Bundle\n- Bundle 的 `bundleId`、`bundleHash`、`codeHash` 和协议版本\n\n原因：\n\n- R8、BlackObfuscator 和 VMP 可能包含随机字典、随机花指令、任务路径或任务级符号。\n- 即使源码、入口和编译参数相同，多次编译的 DEX 与 Bundle 也可能不同。\n- Native Bundle 的 `codeHash` 必须等于目标配置的 `dexHash`；只复制 DEX 会让 VMP 产物缺失。\n- `useLocalCache=true` 只控制宿主运行时缓存，不保证编译产物确定化。\n\n## 推荐 MCP 流程\n\n1. 选择一个基准配置，推送源码并提交一次编译。\n2. 等待任务进入 `SUCCESS`，不要先下载或单配置应用该任务。\n3. 调用 `apply_compile_task_to_configs`：\n\n```json\n{\n  \"taskId\": \"COMPILE_TASK_ID\",\n  \"configIds\": [CONFIG_ID_1, CONFIG_ID_2, CONFIG_ID_3],\n  \"deleteTaskAfterApply\": false\n}\n```\n\n4. 检查返回值：\n\n- `appliedToConfigs=true`\n- `appliedCount` 等于目标配置数量\n- 所有快照的 `files.dexHash` 等于返回的 `dexHash`\n- VMP 开启时所有配置具有相同的 `bundleId` 和 `bundleHash`\n- 每个配置原有的资源 ZIP、包名、版本和业务参数保持不变\n\n5. 验证完成后再删除编译任务记录，或在调用时传 `deleteTaskAfterApply=true`。\n\n## 后端接口\n\n```text\nPOST /api/app-token/compile-tasks/{taskId}/apply-batch\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\"configIds\":[CONFIG_ID_1,CONFIG_ID_2]}\n```\n\n约束：\n\n- 目标配置必须属于编译任务对应的同一个应用。\n- 当前 ApiToken 必须可以访问每个目标配置。\n- `configIds` 必须唯一，单次最多 100 个。\n- 任务必须成功、尚未下载且尚未应用。\n- 后端会锁定任务，预校验 DEX、Bundle 及全部目标配置，再在同一事务中更新配置。\n- 任一目标更新失败时，配置更新整体回滚，任务保持可再次应用。\n- 全部成功后任务才标记为已应用；Native Bundle ZIP 按 `bundleHash` 去重存储。\n\n## 兼容说明\n\n- 未开启 VMP 的任务同样使用批量接口，此时完整产物只有 DEX。\n- `apply_compile_task_to_config` 仍用于单配置发布。\n- `update_config_files(updateDexOnly=true)` 适合手动替换普通 DEX；启用 VMP 时不要用它代替完整产物批量接口。\n- 已经下载或应用的任务临时产物会被清理，不能再拿同一任务执行第二次批量应用。\n"
        },
        {
          "path": "references/project-examples.md",
          "content": "# Verify Project Examples\n\n## 当前项目示例\n\n仅当当前工作目录是 `造梦西游4/verify_cloud_zmxy` 这类项目时使用：\n\n```text\nconfigId: 44\npackageName: org.cocos2dx.zmxy.m4399\nworkspacePath: /Users/yuminghao/Desktop/逆向app/造梦西游手机版/造梦西游4/verify_cloud_zmxy/src\ncurrentFilePath: src/com/xy/zmxy/cloud/Entry.java\ndexClassName: com.xy.zmxy.cloud.Entry\ndexMethodName: main\ndexMethodParamTypes: []\n```\n\n资源 zip 示例：\n\n```text\n/Users/yuminghao/Desktop/逆向app/造梦西游手机版/造梦西游4/verify_cloud_zmxy_native/resHook.zip\n```\n\n发布资源：\n\n```json\n{\n  \"configId\": 44,\n  \"zipPath\": \"/Users/yuminghao/Desktop/逆向app/造梦西游手机版/造梦西游4/verify_cloud_zmxy_native/resHook.zip\",\n  \"maxFileSizeBytes\": 52428800\n}\n```\n\n发布 dex：\n\n```json\n{\n  \"configId\": 44,\n  \"workspacePath\": \"/Users/yuminghao/Desktop/逆向app/造梦西游手机版/造梦西游4/verify_cloud_zmxy/src\",\n  \"currentFilePath\": \"src/com/xy/zmxy/cloud/Entry.java\",\n  \"applyToConfig\": true,\n  \"compileSettings\": {\n    \"dexClassName\": \"com.xy.zmxy.cloud.Entry\",\n    \"dexMethodName\": \"main\",\n    \"dexMethodParamTypes\": [],\n    \"enableR8Obfuscation\": false,\n    \"enableBlackObfuscation\": false,\n    \"useLocalCache\": false\n  }\n}\n```\n\n验证：\n\n```bash\nadb shell pidof org.cocos2dx.zmxy.m4399\nadb shell su -c 'tail -120 /data/data/org.cocos2dx.zmxy.m4399/files/zmxy_hook_trace/runtime-20260621.log' | tr -d '\\r'\nadb shell su -c 'tail -120 /data/data/org.cocos2dx.zmxy.m4399/files/zmxy_hook_trace/native-20260621.log' | tr -d '\\r'\n```\n\n"
        },
        {
          "path": "references/resources-and-modules.md",
          "content": "# Verify Resources And Modules\n\n## 资源 zip 发布\n\nVerify MCP 常用工具：\n\n```text\nmcp__verify.update_config_files\n```\n\nShadowHook 场景优先使用完整安装工具：\n\n```text\nmcp__verify.install_shadowhook\n```\n\n最小 payload：\n\n```json\n{\n  \"configId\": 44,\n  \"runtime\": \"xposed\"\n}\n```\n\n该工具会校验 ShadowHook `2.0.1` AAR/bridge、合并并保留已有 ZIP、生成包装入口、编译、上传\n资源、应用 Dex 并复核 Hash。配置已有 Dex 但没有云源码快照时传 `workspacePath`；只检查本地\n产物时传 `dryRun=true`。自定义 Hook SO 通过 `hookLibraries=[{abi,path}, ...]` 传入，所有选择\n的 ABI 必须具有同名库。\n\n通用 payload：\n\n```json\n{\n  \"configId\": 44,\n  \"zipPath\": \"/absolute/path/to/resHook.zip\",\n  \"maxFileSizeBytes\": 52428800\n}\n```\n\n建议结构：\n\n```text\nresHook.zip\n  payload/lib/arm64-v8a/libxxx.so\n  payload/lib/armeabi-v7a/libxxx.so\n  payload/config/xxx.json\n  payload/assets/...\n```\n\n或：\n\n```text\nresHook.zip\n  lib/arm64-v8a/libxxx.so\n  lib/armeabi-v7a/libxxx.so\n```\n\n云代码读取资源时优先通过 Verify API 找解压目录：\n\n```java\nFile unzipDir = HookHelper.getUnzipDir();\n```\n\n资源加载完成后，如果 Verify 提供清理接口，可在确认当前资源已经复制到宿主私有目录后调用：\n\n```java\nHookHelper.clearZipCache();\n```\n\n这样可以降低旧 zip 缓存干扰。\n\n不要默认从旧 app cache / 历史目录 fallback 加载 native/resource。除非代码显式做版本戳校验，否则 fallback 容易造成“新 dex + 旧 so/旧 jar”的版本不一致。native 资源建议从当前 `HookHelper.getUnzipDir()` 对应目录复制，并覆盖写入宿主私有目录。\n\n## Xposed 模块 APK 下载\n\n当用户需要下载某个 Xposed 应用对应的专属 `ITHook.apk` 时，优先使用 MCP：\n\n```text\nmcp__verify.prepare_ithook_apk\nmcp__verify.download_ithook_apk\n```\n\n常用 payload：\n\n```json\n{\n  \"appId\": 123,\n  \"wait\": true,\n  \"outputPath\": \"/absolute/path/to/downloads\"\n}\n```\n\n语义：\n\n- `prepare_ithook_apk` 只检查状态并触发服务端异步构建，不下载。\n- `download_ithook_apk` 会先 prepare；默认 `wait=true`，会轮询到 `READY` 后下载。\n- `outputPath` 传目录时按服务端文件名保存；传 `.apk` 文件路径时保存为该文件；不传时返回 base64。\n- 需要 ACCOUNT 或 APP 级 `VERIFY_API_TOKEN`；CONFIG 级 Token 无权下载应用级 APK。\n- 应用必须是 `XPOSED` 类型；普通/Dex 应用不会生成 ITHook 模块 APK。\n\n\n"
        },
        {
          "path": "references/runtime-crash-analysis.md",
          "content": "# Verify Runtime Crash Query And Download\n\nUse this reference when the user asks to inspect, search, analyze, export, or download Verify Runtime crash and exit reports from the server. For live `adb logcat`, tombstones, and app-private traces, use `device-debugging.md` instead.\n\n## Data Types\n\n- Problem group: events sharing one 64-character `fingerprint`.\n- Event JSON: structured event data including the redacted stack, attribution, runtime, Dex Hash, ABI, API level, exit reason, and metadata. It remains queryable after the raw attachment expires.\n- Raw report: the decrypted attachment uploaded by the Runtime. Attachments are retained for 7 days and may be absent for some exit events.\n- Group ZIP: up to the latest 100 events, their available raw reports, `events.json`, and `manifest.json`. Raw files are capped at 64 MiB per ZIP.\n\n`manifest.json` reports each raw attachment as:\n\n- `EXPORTED`: included under `raw/`.\n- `NOT_AVAILABLE`: the event has no retained raw attachment.\n- `OMITTED_SIZE_LIMIT`: excluded after the 64 MiB group raw-data limit.\n\n## MCP Workflow\n\n1. Inspect token state with `server_info`.\n2. Set `VERIFY_API_TOKEN` with `set_api_token` when the current process has no application token.\n3. Find the target application with `list_apps` when its `appId` is unknown.\n4. Query problem groups with `list_runtime_crashes`.\n5. Open one group with `get_runtime_crash_events` and select an `eventId`.\n6. Download `raw`, `event`, or `group` with `download_runtime_crash_report`.\n7. Verify the returned local path, byte count, and SHA-256 before analysis.\n\nToken scope rules:\n\n- ACCOUNT token: `appId` is required.\n- APP or CONFIG token: `appId` may be omitted; when supplied it must match the bound application.\n- ProtectToken is for protection tasks and is not used for crash-report access.\n\n## Query Examples\n\nRecent Java crashes attributed to cloud Dex:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"list_runtime_crashes\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"appId\": 7,\n    \"incidentType\": \"JAVA_CRASH\",\n    \"attribution\": \"VERIFY_DEX\",\n    \"days\": 7,\n    \"page\": 1,\n    \"size\": 30\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSearch package names, exception summaries, messages, or Dex Hash prefixes with `query`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"list_runtime_crashes\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"appId\": 7,\n    \"query\": \"com.example.host\",\n    \"days\": 30\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSupported `incidentType` values:\n\n```text\nJAVA_CRASH\nNATIVE_CRASH\nANR\nANR_SUSPECTED\nLOW_MEMORY\nSYSTEM_OR_USER_REQUEST\nINTENTIONAL_RESTART\nABNORMAL_EXIT_UNKNOWN\nDEX_ENTRY_FAILURE\n```\n\nSupported `attribution` values:\n\n```text\nVERIFY_DEX\nVERIFY_RUNTIME\nNPATCH_RUNTIME\nHOST_APP\nUNKNOWN\n```\n\n## Event Inspection\n\nUse the exact fingerprint returned by `list_runtime_crashes`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"get_runtime_crash_events\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"appId\": 7,\n    \"fingerprint\": \"FINGERPRINT_64_HEX\",\n    \"limit\": 50\n  }\n}\n```\n\nCompare these fields before assigning a cause:\n\n- `occurredAt` and `receivedAt` for capture/upload delay.\n- `runtimeType` and `runtimeVersion` for Patch versus Inject behavior.\n- `attribution` and `attributionReasons` for the current classifier result.\n- `dexHash`, `dexClassName`, and `dexMethodName` for the exact cloud payload.\n- `abi` and `apiLevel` for architecture or Android-version clustering.\n- `exceptionClass`, `messageRedacted`, and `stackTraceRedacted` for the failure path.\n- `appExitReason`, `appExitSubReason`, `appExitStatus`, and `importance` for process exits without a Java exception.\n\nTreat attribution as evidence, not proof. Correlate it with the selected event's raw report, device logs, Runtime build label, and Dex Hash.\n\n## Download Examples\n\nDownload the decrypted raw attachment for one event:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"download_runtime_crash_report\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"appId\": 7,\n    \"type\": \"raw\",\n    \"eventId\": \"EVENT_UUID\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nDownload the structured event JSON, including when its raw attachment has expired:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"download_runtime_crash_report\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"appId\": 7,\n    \"type\": \"event\",\n    \"eventId\": \"EVENT_UUID\",\n    \"outputPath\": \"output/crashes\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nDownload a problem-group ZIP:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"download_runtime_crash_report\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"appId\": 7,\n    \"type\": \"group\",\n    \"fingerprint\": \"FINGERPRINT_64_HEX\",\n    \"outputPath\": \"output/crashes/group.zip\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nDownload behavior:\n\n- Default directory: `~/.cache/verify-mcp/downloads/runtime-crashes`.\n- A path with a filename extension is treated as the target file.\n- A path without an extension is treated as a directory and the response filename is used.\n- Keep `includeBase64=false` for normal use. Enable it only when inline bytes are explicitly required.\n- The result returns `fileName`, `size`, `sha256`, response metadata, and `saved.outputPath`.\n\n## Local Verification\n\nAfter a download, inspect the saved artifact rather than asking MCP to inline it:\n\n```bash\nls -lh OUTPUT_PATH\nshasum -a 256 OUTPUT_PATH\nfile OUTPUT_PATH\n```\n\nFor an event JSON:\n\n```bash\njq . OUTPUT_PATH\n```\n\nFor a group ZIP:\n\n```bash\nunzip -l OUTPUT_PATH\nunzip -p OUTPUT_PATH manifest.json | jq .\nunzip -p OUTPUT_PATH events.json | jq 'length'\n```\n\n## REST Fallback\n\nUse this only when the Verify MCP tools are not present in the active session. `VERIFY_BASE_URL` includes the `/verfiy` context path.\n\nQuery groups:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsS \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $VERIFY_API_TOKEN\" \\\n  \"$VERIFY_BASE_URL/api/app-token/runtime-crashes?appId=APP_ID&days=30&page=1&size=30\"\n```\n\nQuery group events:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsS \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $VERIFY_API_TOKEN\" \\\n  \"$VERIFY_BASE_URL/api/app-token/runtime-crashes/groups/FINGERPRINT?appId=APP_ID&limit=50\"\n```\n\nDownload one raw report:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fLJO \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $VERIFY_API_TOKEN\" \\\n  \"$VERIFY_BASE_URL/api/app-token/runtime-crashes/events/EVENT_ID/raw?appId=APP_ID\"\n```\n\nReplace `/raw` with `/export` for event JSON. Use\n`/api/app-token/runtime-crashes/groups/FINGERPRINT/export?appId=APP_ID` for the group ZIP.\n\n## Web Workflow\n\nThe Web page is `/runtime-crashes`. Open a problem group, select an event, then use:\n\n- `导出事件`: structured event JSON.\n- `下载原始报告`: decrypted retained attachment.\n- `读取原始报告`: decrypt and preview without downloading.\n- `导出问题组`: group ZIP with manifest.\n\nWeb access uses the logged-in application's `VIEW_APP` permission. Raw preview and all exports write an access-audit record.\n\n## Failure Handling\n\n- `401`: inspect `server_info`, then set the intended ApiToken and retry.\n- `403`: verify token scope and target application ownership/binding.\n- `账号级 ApiToken 必须指定 appId`: pass the application ID explicitly.\n- `崩溃指纹无效`: use the exact 64-character hexadecimal fingerprint from the list result.\n- `该事件没有原始附件`: export the event JSON; then use device traces if raw evidence is required.\n- Raw download succeeds but group ZIP lacks that report: inspect `manifest.json` for the size-limit status.\n- Empty query results: retry with `days=0`, remove type/attribution filters, then verify the selected `appId`.\n\nDo not infer that report ingestion failed only because a raw attachment is missing. Exit-only events can have structured metadata without a raw file, and retained attachments are cleaned after 7 days.\n"
        },
        {
          "path": "references/verify-framework-guide.md",
          "content": "# Verify Framework Reference Index\n\nThe original combined guide is split into task-specific references so unrelated material does not enter context.\n\n- Core concepts and tokens: `core-and-tokens.md`\n- Cloud-code publishing: `cloud-code-publish.md`\n- Compile troubleshooting: `compile-troubleshooting.md`\n- Dex cache runtime: `dex-cache-runtime.md`\n- Multi-config Dex publishing: `multi-config-publishing.md`\n- Resources and modules: `resources-and-modules.md`\n- MenuPro integration: `menupro-integration.md`\n- Persistent WiFi ADB Root: `wifi-adb-root.md`\n- MCP tool catalog: `mcp-tools.md`\n- Device debugging: `device-debugging.md`\n- Local Patch Runtime: `local-patch-runtime.md`\n- Card heartbeat verification: `heartbeat-verification.md`\n- Local runtime protection: `local-protection.md`\n- Project examples: `project-examples.md`\n\nStart from `../SKILL.md`, choose the narrowest matching reference, and add another reference only when the task crosses that boundary.\n"
        },
        {
          "path": "references/wifi-adb-root.md",
          "content": "# Verify Persistent WiFi ADB Root\n\n## Persistent WiFi ADB Root 模块批量安装\n\n使用场景：Root Android 设备需要开机常驻固定 ADB TCP 端口，并希望通过 MCP 自动识别 Root 管理器、批量安装、立即生效，不进入管理器页面手动刷入。\n\n工具：\n\n```text\nmcp__verify.install_wifi_adb_module\n```\n\n准备条件：\n\n- MCP 主机已安装 `adb`；可通过 `VERIFY_ADB_PATH` 指定可执行文件。\n- 目标出现在 `adb devices`，状态为 `device`。\n- `adb shell su -c id` 返回 `uid=0`。\n- 当前 MCP 进程已配置 `VERIFY_API_TOKEN`，用于读取服务端模块清单和 ZIP。\n\n支持矩阵：\n\n```text\nMAGISK          Magisk 官方版/测试版              magisk --install-module ZIP\nMAGISK_ALPHA    Magisk Alpha                      magisk --install-module ZIP\nKITSUNE_MASK    Kitsune Mask / Magisk Delta       magisk --install-module ZIP\nKERNELSU        KernelSU                          /data/adb/ksud module install ZIP\nKERNELSU_NEXT   KernelSU Next                     /data/adb/ksud module install ZIP\nSUKISU_ULTRA    SukiSU Ultra                      /data/adb/ksud module install ZIP\nAPATCH          APatch                            /data/adb/apd module install ZIP\n```\n\nRoot 管理器的兼容分支只要继续提供同一底层 CLI，也会复用对应安装引擎。SuperSU、phh-su 等只有 Root shell、没有上述模块引擎的设备会返回设备级错误，不会直接写未知模块目录。\n\n先检查全部在线设备：\n\n```json\n{\n  \"dryRun\": true,\n  \"concurrency\": 3\n}\n```\n\n安装到全部在线设备并立即启用 `5555`：\n\n```json\n{\n  \"port\": 5555,\n  \"concurrency\": 3,\n  \"reboot\": false,\n  \"force\": false\n}\n```\n\n只处理指定设备：\n\n```json\n{\n  \"serials\": [\"USB_SERIAL\", \"192.168.1.20:37123\"],\n  \"port\": 5555,\n  \"concurrency\": 2\n}\n```\n\n执行顺序：\n\n1. 获取最新版清单；正式安装时下载一次 ZIP 并校验大小、SHA-256、ZIP 中央目录和必需脚本。\n2. 读取所有目标的 Root、Android API、IPv4、Root 管理器和已有模块版本。\n3. 为每台设备建立独立临时目录，调用对应管理器 CLI 安装。\n4. 写入 `/data/adb/wifi-adbd/config.conf`，用独立脚本准备持久属性。\n5. 主机调用 `adb tcpip PORT` 热重启 `adbd`，随后连接 `IP:PORT`。\n6. 检查模块版本、端口属性、`adbd` 状态和监听端口，最后清理临时文件。\n\n结果判断：\n\n- `success=true`：整个批次的所有目标都成功。\n- `devices[].success`：单台最终状态；批量场景必须逐项读取。\n- `installed=true`：Root 管理器已经接受模块。\n- `activated=true`：已执行热激活。\n- `verified=true`：WiFi 地址重连和健康检查完成。\n- `rebootRequired=true`：模块已安装，但热激活或重连未完成，后续启动时由模块服务接管。\n- `manager` 是具体发行版，`managerEngine` 是实际安装引擎。\n\n默认不重启。显式传 `reboot=true` 时，只在单台安装、热激活和验证都成功后请求该设备重启。单台失败不会中止其他设备，最终报告成功、失败和需重启数量。\n\n\n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "verify-shadowhook",
